        {
          "id": 3428537236,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "There are two signals: textEdited() and textChanged() (see https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qlineedit.html#textChanged). textChanged would also fire if the text changed through the app changing it (which I would assume would include clear() ). textEdited() does fire with the backspace as well as long as there was a change to the text inside the QLineEdit (which also includes the change from 1 char to an empty field). \n\nThe reason I went with Edited is, because validation and completion are both actions that occur whilst the textfield is being changed by the user. So it just felt the more correct choice. In the end I think it should not matter. I usually go with textChanged in other cases, but was not aware of the clear() issue that textEdited would bring.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
